/*
claude says:

test import and linked files.
this is a SECOND library header, imported alongside library.slh.

its job is the OWNER-COMPUTED layout: an incomplete class whose completion hides
fields whose sizes live in ANOTHER module. Pack's completer (extra.sl) cannot
fold Pack's size at compile time — it is `constant + @Rope__$sizeof` — so it
exports @Pack__$sizeof as a zero word and fills it in its layout init, which the
preamble at the top of consumer's main runs. Two modules must exist for that,
which is why this header does. consumer.sl imports it and reads every value
back through Pack's methods.
*/

/* incomplete class; its completion in extra.sl hides library.slh's Rope (an
   imported opaque class) and LPack (a computed-layout class over Rope). */
Pack(int a_ = 1, ...) {
    _(); ~();
    int total();
}
